AssetStudio -- https://github.com/Razviar/assetstudio (MIT)
  Copyright (c) Perfare, RazTools, Razviar
  Source of truth for AssetBundle, SerializedFile, TypeTree and class layout,
  for the plain texture format conversion (Texture2DConverter.cs, Half.cs),
  for which block or Crunch decoder each texture format goes to
  (Texture2DConverter.cs), for the Xbox 360 byte swap (Texture2DConverter.cs),
  for the vertical flip (Texture2DExtensions.cs), and for sprites: the crop,
  the packing rotation, the tight-mesh mask and the variant-atlas resize step
  (SpriteHelper.cs, Mesh.cs).

ImageSharp.Drawing -- https://github.com/SixLabors/ImageSharp.Drawing
  (Apache License 2.0, full text in LICENSE-APACHE)
  Copyright (c) Six Labors
  The triangle fill of the tight-mesh mask in src/sprite.ts is derived from
  ImageSharp.Drawing v1.0.0-beta15, the version AssetStudio fills sprite
  meshes with, so that the mask matches AssetStudio's to the pixel. It is a
  modified TypeScript translation of parts of:
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/ScanEdge.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/ScanEdgeCollection.Build.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/RasterizerExtensions.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/PolygonScanner.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/ActiveEdgeList.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/InternalPath.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Helpers/TopologyUtilities.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Processing/Processors/Drawing/FillPathProcessor{TPixel}.cs
  Changes: translated from C# to TypeScript; cut down to filling one closed
  triangle without antialiasing, with the odd-even rule, into a 0/1 mask;
  the memory pools, sorting helpers and span types are replaced by arrays.
  That code, and only that code, is under the Apache License 2.0; the rest
  of this package is under the MIT License (LICENSE).

UnityPy -- https://github.com/K0lb3/UnityPy (MIT)
  Copyright (c) K0lb3
  Secondary reference and oracle used to generate the test goldens. Source of
  the Switch texture deswizzle (helpers/TextureSwizzler.py,
  export/Texture2DConverter.py) and of a sprite's alpha texture merge, ETC1
  split alpha (export/SpriteHelper.py, get_image), which AssetStudio does not
  have.

